  "Id": 3404,
  "Title": "\u200bCIME Launches Capacity Building Programme to Enhance Emergency Medical Training Across Pakistan\u200b",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "CIME's capacity-building training program aims to improve emergency care in Pakistan by empowering healthcare professionals. This effort reflects CIME's commitment to enhancing community health and fostering support within the healthcare sector.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClass1DB3FE0572744FC1B2E3E11E4D31F788\"><p>CIME has taken an initiative by launching a capacity building programme to provide medical emergency training to doctors and nurses of medical centres across Pakistan. This project aims to extend CIME's expertise to benefit community healthcare facilities across the country, showcasing CIME's dedication to giving back to the community.\u200b<br></p><p>This collaboration with Fidai Medical Centre marks the beginning of a series of similar efforts, as CIME plans to organize training sessions for other medical facilities in the future. By imparting essential knowledge and skills for handling medical emergencies, CIME aims to empower healthcare professionals to deliver effective care, ultimately improving health outcomes for the communities they serve.<br></p><p>Through these collaborative efforts, CIME seeks to foster a culture of mutual support within the healthcare sector, enhancing healthcare delivery and outcomes nationwide. This initiative reflects CIME's core values of compassion, professionalism, and dedication to building a better society.<br></p><p>\u200b<br></p></div>",
